# Used by Wrangler in local development. Copy to .dev.vars and fill in.
# In production, set these as Cloudflare Worker secrets instead.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:8787
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-32-plus-random-chars-for-local-dev
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Local QA only: open lessons beyond Unit 1 + scoring on localhost
# (qa-audio.mjs needs this), skipping the subscription gate.
# Never set in production.
# PAYWALL_DISABLED=1
# Stripe billing (Lesson 5+ paywall: $3/month or $29/year). Create the
# two recurring Prices in Stripe, then set all four values. In
# production use `wrangler secret put` for the two keys; the Price IDs
# are not secret but are kept here for parity. Point the Stripe webhook
# at https://nicelingo.com/api/billing/webhook for
# checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.* and
# invoice.payment_failed. Without these, /billing shows plans but
# checkout, portal, and status return 503/401 as appropriate.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# STRIPE_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID=
# STRIPE_YEARLY_PRICE_ID=
# One-time THB PromptPay pass prices (THB 99 / 30 days, THB 990 / 365
# days, no recurring interval). Thailand-only on the billing page.
# STRIPE_PROMPTPAY_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID=
# STRIPE_PROMPTPAY_YEARLY_PRICE_ID=
# Recurring THB card prices for Thai visitors, mirroring PromptPay
# (THB 99/month, THB 990/year). Non-Thai checkouts keep the USD prices.
# STRIPE_THB_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID=
# STRIPE_THB_YEARLY_PRICE_ID=
# Optional: a Nicelingo-specific Customer Portal configuration (plan
# switching between the two prices above). Without it Stripe's default
# portal configuration for the account is used.
# STRIPE_PORTAL_CONFIGURATION_ID=
# MailNice (transactional email for verification + password reset, via
# api.mailnice.net like Blognice). When both are set, email verification
# becomes required at sign-up; until then accounts activate immediately
# and no mail is sent.
# MAILNICE_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM=Nicelingo <support@mailer.nicelingo.com>
# Optional, only for reading analytics back (usageReport): a Cloudflare
# token with Account Analytics Read. Event writes need no token.
# CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=
